ith the taliban to be  able to remove  thousands of people from that airport  over the next week or so what are the  chances of that deal having been struck  already and we'll never know what was  what if it had been what what price had  been paid  yeah  i i i hope the probability is low i pray  that it is uh  maybe they've got that done might but  that would that would actually uh  suggest that they actually had a plan  you talked about all the planning and  contingencies you don't put four or five  six thousand people back in for  something you've planned for after you  just took them out this is clearly  unplanned activity i'd be surprised if  they have that kind of agreement and if  they do i want to know what it is this  is going to cost the united states of  america in terms of our  morality in terms of the risk from the  rest of the world  laura i've said this time and time again  we we had a deterrence model we knew  that strength created peace and we know  that weakness begets war you are seeing  the summers the you're seeing the some  result of the weakness of the  administration whether it's our southern  border whether it's handing the russians  a pipeline completion  that can threaten europe all of these  things the whole world watches chairman  kim xi xingping they are all watching  what's happening today and i hope this  administration comes to understand that  apologizing placating appeasing being  weak only presents risks to american  security  yesterday in an interview liz cheney had  something to say about you sir watch  president biden bears responsibility for  making this decision  but there is no question that president  trump his administration secretary  pompeo they also bear very significant  responsibility for this they walk down  this path of legitimizing the taliban  the notion of we're going to end endless  wars that campaign slogan what we're  watching right now in afghanistan is  what happens when america withdraws from  the world  uh 